-- title:
--   Small-rate atlas parameter data
-- statement:
--   Fix a carrier base $m$, dimension $d$, distinguished coordinate $i$, and tolerance $\eta$. The parameter record contains integer scales $L_j\ge32\cdot61^d$, a height $K$, a common joint bound $J$, and one normalized contraction family for widths at most $6L_i$. Every literal rank rate at stage $d+1$ is required to satisfy
--
--   $$ C_j^{(d+1)}<\eta. $$
--
--   This packages the quantitative data needed to evaluate a single canonical family across every action point.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (2026), Section(s) 6 / Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.39824v1. This item is auxiliary infrastructure of the accompanying formalization, not a claim that each implementation definition is separately numbered in the paper. Original Lean module AbelianTargets/AtlasScaleParameters.lean, selected declaration lines 15-29; SHA-256 1c9bffd39e0214fe5d6a7724cd54ae89ad4e0620ab46a3004554f16c6efaadac. Selected spans are from the final generated manifest. The original source snapshot is local; no public repository URL or commit was available.

